Q9 — Agentic Architecture / Delegation

A financial-analysis agent receives a request requiring information from regulatory filings, market data, and internal company documents. Three specialized worker agents handle those sources.

Each worker produces a well-supported answer, but the coordinator sometimes combines individually correct facts into a globally inconsistent conclusion because the workers used different reporting periods, definitions, and assumptions.

What’s the best architectural improvement?

A. Require every worker to produce longer reasoning traces so the coordinator has more information for synthesis.

B. Have each worker independently produce the final recommendation and use majority voting.

C. Before delegation, establish a shared analysis contract defining relevant periods, entity definitions, units, assumptions, and required provenance; have the coordinator validate worker outputs against that contract before synthesis.

D. Have each worker read every other worker’s complete output and recursively revise its own analysis until all three agree.

